-- title:
--   Base change commutes with fixed fields of q-expansion fields
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero (hence a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra), and write $\iota =$ [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) for the ring homomorphism $\mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!) \to L(\!(q)\!)$ obtained by applying $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ to every coefficient of a Laurent series. For an intermediate field $F$ of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$, [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L F`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) denotes the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L(\!(q)\!)$ generated over $L$ by $\iota(F)$. Let $F_1 \le F_0$ be intermediate fields of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathbb{Q}(\!(q)\!)$, let $G$ be a finite group, and let $\delta : G \to \operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(F_0)$ be a homomorphism into the group of $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of $F_0$, such that an element $y \in F_0$ lies in $F_1$ precisely when $\delta(g)(y) = y$ for all $g \in G$. Let $\delta_L : G \to \operatorname{Aut}_L(L \cdot F_0)$ be a homomorphism into the $L$-algebra automorphisms of $L \cdot F_0 =$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L F₀`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), compatible with $\delta$ in the sense that $\delta_L(g)(\iota y) = \iota(\delta(g) y)$ inside $L(\!(q)\!)$ for all $g \in G$ and $y \in F_0$. Then for every $x \in L \cdot F_0$ one has $\delta_L(g)(x) = x$ for all $g \in G$ if and only if $x$, viewed in $L(\!(q)\!)$, lies in [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L F₁`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. in $L \cdot F_1$.
--
--   This is the statement that forming the compositum with $L$ commutes with passing to the fixed field of a finite group of automorphisms, in the setting of subfields of the Laurent series field generated by $q$-expansions: $(L \cdot F_0)^G = L \cdot F_0^G$. It is used in the construction of the diamond action on the function field of the modular curve over $L$, where the invariant subfield of $L \cdot \mathbb{Q}(X_1(Mp))$ is identified with $L \cdot \mathbb{Q}(X_0(Mp))$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_forall_algEquiv_laurentBaseChange_apply_eq_iff_mem_laurentBaseChange_of_fixedField.lean

